// Hearthwood - CLASS PROMOTIONS (XCOM / Fire Emblem style).
// At Level 3 a hero promotes into one of TWO advanced classes of its
// NATURAL class (the one it was born with - a Class Collar never changes
// it). At Level 5 it either MASTERS that path (rank II) or CROSS-TRAINS
// and also learns the other path's signature skill.
// Pure data - Studio-editable (Hearthwood Studio > ⚜ Promotions).
// Rules: services/heartwood/promotions.js; skills run in tacticsClasses.js.
//
// A promotion grants:
//   stats   - { hp, attack } bump (always, even while wearing a collar)
//   skill   - a strong new class skill (often ALL-IN). Generic `kind`s:
//             smite (big hit on one enemy), nova (hits every enemy around
//             it), volley (hits every enemy in range), sanctuary (heals /
//             shields allies around it), rally (empowers allies around it),
//             blink (teleports next to an enemy and hits it), knock (hits
//             and knocks the enemy back N tiles - into hazards!), zone
//             (hits a 3x3 area and changes the ground: fire / poison /
//             spikes / ice / bush). `fx` = the usual skill-tree riders.
//             `pct` = resource price as % of the bar (ALL-IN skills need
//             at least that and spend everything).
//   passive - an upgraded passive on top of the class's own: `mods` = a
//             conditional bonus (same keys as traits.js `mods`).
//   twist   - the RESOURCE twist: maxPct (+% bigger bar), startPct (starts
//             fuller), regen (+resource each turn, 100-bar amount), bp (a
//             new breakpoint: { at, name, dmg | aim | heal | guard | cheaper | skillPct }).
//   master  - rank II (Level 5): `patch` = new skill numbers, `text`.

